{"version":3,"term":{"cols":100,"rows":30,"type":"xterm-256color"},"timestamp":1791840486,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":"asciiverse/adventures/stories/stage/curses/curses","env":{"TERM":"xterm-256color","LANG":"C.UTF-8","COLORTERM":"truecolor"}}
[0.013, "o", "\u001b[?1049h\u001b[22;0;0t\u001b[1;30r\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4l\u001b[?7h\u001b[?1h\u001b="]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[4;26H\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m                                                \u001b[5;26H"]
[0.000, "o", "  Let Rome in Tiber melt, and the wide arch     \u001b[6;26H"]
[0.000, "o", "  Of the ranged empire fall! Here is my space.  \u001b[7;26H"]
[0.000, "o", "  Kingdoms are clay.                            \u001b[8;26H"]
[0.000, "o", "                                                \u001b[9;26H  -- Shakespeare, \"Antony and Cleopatra\" I:1    \u001b[10;26H"]
[0.000, "o", "                                                \u001b[14;40H\u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[1K "]
[0.000, "o", "Welcome to CURSES\u001b[17;35H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[m[Please press SPACE to begin.]\r\u001b[18d"]
[2.495, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m Attic                                                          Score: 0                            \u001b[2;1H (in Meldrew Hall)                                              Turns: 1           June 3rd, 1993   \u001b[4;1H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[5d"]
[0.000, "o", "It's become a matter of pride now not to give up. That tourist map of Paris must be up here\r\u001b[6d"]
[0.000, "o", "somewhere in all this clutter, even if it has been five years since your last trip. And it's your\r\u001b[7down fault. It looks as if your great-grandfather was the last person to tidy up these lofts...\r\u001b[8d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[K\u001b[9d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;1mCURSES\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\u001b[10d"]
[0.000, "o", "An Interactive Diversion\u001b[K\r\u001b[11dCopyright (c) 1993, 1994, 1995 by Graham Nelson.\r\u001b[12d"]
[0.000, "o", "Release 16 / Serial number 951024 / Inform v1600 Library 5/12\r\u001b[13dStandard interpreter 1.1\r\u001b[14d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[K\u001b[15d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;1mAttic\r\u001b[16d\u001b(B\u001b[mThe attics, full of low beams and awkward angles, begin here in a relatively tidy area which extends\u001b[17;1H"]
[0.000, "o", "north, south and east. The wooden floorboards seem fairly sound, just as well considering how heavy\r\u001b[18dall these teachests are. But the old wiring went years ago, and there's no electric light.\r\u001b[20d"]
[0.000, "o", "A hinged trapdoor in the floor stands open, and light streams in from below.\r\u001b[21dWarning: @get_child called with object 0 (PC = 280fb) (will ignore further occurrences)\r\u001b[23d>"]
[2.526, "o", "i"]
[0.090, "o", "n"]
